- **Are the current figures enough?** No. The 5-figure summary covers about 6 of the 14 major findings, almost all from the simulated-water side. It leaves out how overhead power actually behaves, whether the power models change decisions, the Prineville check (the project's only measured water evidence), and the Step 30 result.
- **Should we list the findings first?** Yes. The figure set was chosen from a plan written before Steps 29–30 had results, and that is why the gaps and a stale claim got in. A one-page list of findings makes coverage checkable: each figure should prove exactly one row of it.
- **Two documentation errors to fix:**
